# Project rules (always on)

- Read `AGENTS.md` first. The Jira issue (`INT-xxx`) defines the scope. `docs/` defines what to build.
- **Billing model (two levels):** monthly participant statement (not payable) + legal invoices per producer→consumer pair (self-billing mandate in T&C), netted per pair, threshold per pair (default 5 EUR/CHF, carried forward, forced at year end or exit). Direct charge on the producer's Stripe Connect account; payout once period invoices where the participant is producer are Paid. The platform never holds funds. Grid fee / levy / tax lines come from the tariff port; 0 with a mention when no DSO tariff is published (REQ-004, REQ-007).
- **V1 scope:** live mode per community (operator + live Stripe keys), Greenvolt first; others virtual (Stripe test). EWDS Client Gateway adapters are real, selected by environment variables; mock is the default until EWAG grants roles/topics.
- Language of code, comments, docs and commits: **English**.
- Business rules BR-01..BR-15 (`docs/architecture/01-functional-architecture.md` §6) are mandatory. Cite the rule id in code comments where a rule is implemented.
- Do not invent requirements. If something is missing or contradictory in `docs/`, stop and state it in the PR description (proposed spec change).
- Never read or modify `brain/` or `docs/project-context/` (confidential, not in Git).
- Do not attribute work to a coding assistant or an editor product in source, documentation, comments, commit messages, notices, or generated files. Do not add a Co-authored-by trailer for one. Credit stays with Blooo and the INTELLIGENT project.
